323:        "value" : "This dataset contains the measurement results from white blood cells from 3 whole blood samples collected into citrate buffer. For phenotyping experiments, 500 micro litre of whole blood was placed in a 15 milli litre falcon tube, so that approximately 2,000,000 WBCs were stained with the following antibody cocktail: CD15 FITC (BD, cat no:  332778, clone MMA, 5 micro litre per test), Siglec8 Pe (Biolegend, cat no: 347104, clone 7C9), CD14 PeCF594 (BD, cat no: 562334, clone M phi $9, 5 micro litre per test), CD19 PerCP-CY5.5 (BD, cat no 340951, clone SJ25C1, 20 micro litre per test), CD3 BV421 (BD, cat no: 562426, clone UCHT1, 5 micro litre per test), CD45 V500 (BD, cat no: 647450, clone 2D1, 5 micro litre per test), CD4 BV605 (BD, cat no: 562658, clone RPA-T4, 5 micro litre per test), CD56 APC (BD, cat no: 341025, clone NCAM16.2, 5 micro litre per test) and CD8 APC-CY7 (BD, cat no: 557834, clone SK1, 5 micro litre test). Whole blood was incubated with the staining cocktail for 1 hour on ice after which red blood cell (RBC) lysis was performed by the addition of 4.5 milli litre of 1x BD FACS lysis solution (cat no: 349202) prepared from a 10x stock in reagent grade water (SIGMA, cat no: W4502).  Lysis was carried out for 10 minutes at room temperature in the dark.  Samples were then spun down at 500 gran for 5 minutes and washed twice in 50 milli litre of wash buffer (PBS + 2% FBS).  Samples were re-suspended in a final volume of 60 micro litre of wash buffer and transferred to 1.5 milli litre Eppendorf tubes for acquisition.\n\nEight different white blood cell types were phenotyped with this panel: CD4+/CD8+ T-cells, neutrophils, monocytes, B-cells, CD56+ NKT-cells, other NKT-cells and eosinophils. See Figure~\\ref{fig:gating} for an overview of the gating process."
